id=a52sxq_aod_brightness_slider
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: AOD brightness choice
author=kusti420
description=Settings > Lock screen and AOD > "AOD brightness": Automatic (default), Automatic brighter, or a fixed 2 / 10 / 30 / 60 nit - the four low-power levels of the S6E3FC3 panel, like the 4-step slider the stock A52s had in its AOD settings. One UI 9 moved Samsung's own slider to Good Lock's LockStar and AODService cannot be patched without losing its Samsung signature, so SystemUI's AODScreenBrightness.updateDozeBrightness passes the level AODService asks for through K4AodBrightness.apply(), which reads persist.sys.k4.aod_brightness (0 automatic, 1-4 fixed level, 5 one step brighter). Automatic already matches the stock thresholds (patches/aod_brightness). A new value applies at the next AOD start or light change.
